### Block 10 - Concurrency in JPA: @Version and locks
### Select the "local" environment. Every demo uses its own temporary product.

### Two users, same row. B reads, A changes and commits, B tries to commit.
### Q: what version did A and B load? What happened to B? What would happen without @Version?
POST {{host}}/demo/locking/optimistic?initialStock=10

### Controlled retry: a conflict is injected on the first attempt
### Q: why must the retry start a NEW transaction and reload the entity?
POST {{host}}/demo/locking/optimistic-retry?increment=5&maxAttempts=3

### Not enough attempts: set maxAttempts=1 and the retry never happens
POST {{host}}/demo/locking/optimistic-retry?increment=5&maxAttempts=1

### Pessimistic locking: A holds the lock, B does not wait
### Q: when is this better than @Version? What does it cost?
POST {{host}}/demo/locking/pessimistic

### @Version also protects the naive PUT from block 4:
### the incoming object has version 0, so once the product has been updated the merge is rejected (409).
### Note the "version" field in the response, it grows with every UPDATE.
GET {{host}}/products/{{productId}}

###
PUT {{host}}/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Replaced by PUT",
  "stock": 5
}
